		<li id="LI_C2629BF8C5694BBB8CF4DE42CA9870BB" class="- topic/li "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">Memory Map Initialization at Root Complex:</b> 
		  <p class="- topic/p "> IOC is the home of Device0 configuration space. Memory map registers in Device0 configuration space should be programmed and locked appropriately by BIOS. In HW, these registers are duplicated in multiple locations (IOC/CCF). BIOS will program these registers in IOC ( column 2) for Root complex and NGU is handled by IMR1M programming. HW handles updating all the copies by multicast mechanism. 
		  </p> 
