		<li id="LI_2BFDC774493B4AFBBD68801AB4DB3800" class="- topic/li "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">IOMMU and VTD Configuration:</b> 
		  <p class="- topic/p "> Device IOMMUs like GFX IOMMU, IPU IOMMU are removed and IOMMUs are only present in IOC. 
			  
		  </p> 
		  <ol id="GUID-266ACBAE-91F0-4CD9-A7CF-CB6A8FA00498" class="- topic/ol "> 
			 <li id="LI_A5E4B9718F79431B83A50224EBDD0F58" class="- topic/li ">Gfx IOMMU - Only used by Device2 IPs (GT, Media, Display) 
			 </li> 
			 <li id="LI_7DA990ACD16548A4835F7A7FC4FEA493" class="- topic/li ">Non-Gfx IOMMU - Used by all other devices 
			 </li> 
		  </ol> 
		  <p class="- topic/p "> Refer to 
			 <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-2CAFA02C-9B6D-40A3-81F9-699F83791D5D.xml#GUID-2CAFA02C-9B6D-40A3-81F9-699F83791D5D" class="- topic/xref "></xref> for BIOS requirement. 
		  </p> 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_18D5C472106A4FF8891E207118529DD8" class="- topic/li "><b class="+ topic/ph hi-d/b ">Deprecate WRC Programming:</b> 
		  <p class="- topic/p "> Unlike previous programs, WRC module is now merged with IOC and is always enabled. BIOS had an option to enable/disable WRC feature using CAPID register and does initialization for VC Enable, Allocate, CLOS register (IOTG). This can be deprecated, and BIOS should remove any WRC specific programming code. 
		  </p> 
